1
00:01:27,866 --> 00:01:33,705
THE RYOTSU WAY TO PASS TESTS

2
00:01:40,812 --> 00:01:42,681
"OZAKI MODEL SHOP"

3
00:01:43,114 --> 00:01:46,084
Wow! It's so cool!

4
00:01:46,284 --> 00:01:51,556
TXR-002 Robojack, 40,000 yen.

5
00:01:53,525 --> 00:01:57,362
-There's no way we can buy it. -Not even close.

6
00:01:59,431 --> 00:02:03,969
I don't have any money before payday, either.

7
00:02:06,872 --> 00:02:08,540
-Oops! -Wait!

8
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:11,042
Hold it, Junpei and Kappei!

9
00:02:12,978 --> 00:02:15,447
You're wasting time here again!

10
00:02:15,847 --> 00:02:17,516
Don't you have to study, Junpei?

11
00:02:17,716 --> 00:02:19,117
You have tests tomorrow.

12
00:02:19,618 --> 00:02:25,590
Yeah, but even if I start now, I won't be smart suddenly.

13
00:02:26,958 --> 00:02:27,959
That's true.

14
00:02:28,159 --> 00:02:29,561
-Ryo-san! -Yikes!

15
00:02:30,095 --> 00:02:33,465
Seriously, a grown adult hanging out with kids!

16
00:02:33,999 --> 00:02:35,800
What's so good about a toy?

17
00:02:36,401 --> 00:02:41,773
It's a masterpiece of a full-action robot with a four-channel radio controller.

18
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:45,810
Some people will understand, and some people won't.

19
00:02:46,011 --> 00:02:48,446
Hmm, is that how it goes?

20
00:02:48,647 --> 00:02:55,453
If Junpei could get at least 80 on a test, I'd buy as many of those as he wanted.

21
00:02:55,654 --> 00:02:57,155
Oh, really?

22
00:02:57,355 --> 00:02:58,823
As many as I want?

23
00:02:59,157 --> 00:03:01,626
I-It's just an example.

24
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:04,496
There's no way you'd get 80.

25
00:03:05,797 --> 00:03:06,898
Yeah...

26
00:03:07,198 --> 00:03:08,266
Junpei...

27
00:03:08,466 --> 00:03:10,468
-If you try, you can do it! -What?

28
00:03:10,669 --> 00:03:12,571
Look at Nagashima's Giants this year!

29
00:03:12,771 --> 00:03:18,276
They overcame an 11.5-game gap to win a miraculous league title!

30
00:03:18,476 --> 00:03:21,046
People can do anything if they put their minds to it.

31
00:03:21,279 --> 00:03:25,984
If Junpei gets 80, will you really buy that RC?

32
00:03:27,586 --> 00:03:29,921
Well, I guess so...

33
00:03:30,121 --> 00:03:32,023
-Okay, it's decided! -What?

34
00:03:32,290 --> 00:03:34,993
-Let's go, Junpei, Kappei! -Yeah!

35
00:03:35,193 --> 00:03:36,928
Hey, Ryo-san!

36
00:03:37,128 --> 00:03:39,764
Ryo-san, wait!

37
00:03:39,965 --> 00:03:40,799
Jeez...

38
00:03:40,999 --> 00:03:44,035
-What are we gonna do? -What is it?

39
00:03:44,502 --> 00:03:45,971
Just leave it to me!

40
00:03:46,171 --> 00:03:49,708
But in return, when you get that RC, lend it to me for free.

41
00:03:49,941 --> 00:03:50,542
Sure!

42
00:03:52,243 --> 00:03:55,413
I'll do it! I'll definitely do it!

43
00:04:00,151 --> 00:04:02,520
What? A tutor?

44
00:04:03,555 --> 00:04:05,824
What's that about a tutor?

45
00:04:06,024 --> 00:04:07,359
Why you, Ryotsu?

46
00:04:07,559 --> 00:04:10,695
In the first place, can you be a tutor, Ryo-chan?

47
00:04:10,895 --> 00:04:11,730
What?

48
00:04:12,163 --> 00:04:13,198
Don't mock me!

49
00:04:13,398 --> 00:04:16,401
What kinda fool can't handle elementary school study!

50
00:04:16,634 --> 00:04:18,036
-Let's get started! -Ugh!

51
00:04:18,236 --> 00:04:20,805
But the tests are tomorrow, aren't they?

52
00:04:21,006 --> 00:04:24,743
So, from now, we're gonna study 24 hours without sleeping.

53
00:04:24,976 --> 00:04:25,810
Eh!

54
00:04:26,077 --> 00:04:27,345
That's crazy...

55
00:04:27,545 --> 00:04:28,980
Crazy, lazy, whatever!

56
00:04:29,381 --> 00:04:30,982
For my high school entrance exams,

57
00:04:31,182 --> 00:04:34,452
I studied for three days without sleeping and passed with flying colors!

58
00:04:34,686 --> 00:04:36,554
Without sleeping at all?

59
00:04:36,755 --> 00:04:38,556
Why did you do such a thing?

60
00:04:38,757 --> 00:04:42,394
If I slept, I'd forget everything I'd memorized!

61
00:04:42,594 --> 00:04:43,828
That's extreme.

62
00:04:44,029 --> 00:04:47,666
But people usually can't stay focused that long, right?

63
00:04:47,866 --> 00:04:52,370
Yes, even at work, they say it's more efficient to take a break.

64
00:04:52,704 --> 00:04:54,472
Foolish! That's for average guys.

65
00:04:54,706 --> 00:04:56,541
In my case, my stamina's on another level.

66
00:04:56,741 --> 00:04:59,044
Common sense doesn't apply to me!

67
00:05:01,079 --> 00:05:04,015
It'd be more accurate to say he has no common sense...

68
00:05:04,215 --> 00:05:05,617
All right, listen up.

69
00:05:06,084 --> 00:05:11,122
Most people build up their pace, then burn out.

70
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:19,397
But in my case, I start at full throttle from day one,

71
00:05:19,597 --> 00:05:23,568
then charge straight into the exam.

72
00:05:25,637 --> 00:05:27,705
You have amazing focus!

73
00:05:27,906 --> 00:05:29,140
It's incredible!

74
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:30,642
If you try, you can do it!

75
00:05:31,076 --> 00:05:35,146
Average guys think they're focused, but their minds still wander.

76
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:39,617
In my case, every nerve, from my brain to my fingertips, is locked onto the test.

77
00:05:40,051 --> 00:05:42,287
Mind, body, and spirit, 100% focused!

78
00:05:42,487 --> 00:05:46,758
But if I lose focus even for a second, it all crashes down to zero.

79
00:05:46,958 --> 00:05:47,792
I see.

80
00:05:48,126 --> 00:05:49,761
It's like a human-powered aircraft.

81
00:05:49,961 --> 00:05:51,262
That sounds like Ryo-chan.

82
00:05:51,463 --> 00:05:54,799
So, from now, I'm gonna start training them in my own way...

83
00:05:54,999 --> 00:05:57,669
Hey, where'd they go?

84
00:05:59,370 --> 00:06:01,005
-Wow, great! -What?

85
00:06:01,272 --> 00:06:02,107
Oh, no!

86
00:06:03,641 --> 00:06:04,776
Ah, I knew it!

87
00:06:04,976 --> 00:06:06,978
My hidden plastic models!

88
00:06:07,178 --> 00:06:09,481
Wait a minute, hey!

89
00:06:09,681 --> 00:06:11,182
-Don't touch them! -Why not?

90
00:06:11,850 --> 00:06:15,019
Is he really going to tutor them?

91
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:17,388
I understand his focus is impressive,

92
00:06:17,622 --> 00:06:20,125
but academic ability is a different matter.

93
00:06:20,325 --> 00:06:25,163
Seriously, how on earth does Ryo-san end up as a tutor?

94
00:06:25,396 --> 00:06:26,798
Who knows?

95
00:06:27,465 --> 00:06:29,033
Stop playing, kids.

96
00:06:29,234 --> 00:06:32,203
-Are we really gonna study? -Study?

97
00:06:33,037 --> 00:06:36,708
Of course. We'd go through fire and water for that RC, right?

98
00:06:37,108 --> 00:06:39,878
Bring out your workbooks! What's on the tests?

99
00:06:43,681 --> 00:06:46,651
Okay, let's start with Japanese.

100
00:06:46,851 --> 00:06:48,653
Well, what's this?

101
00:06:48,853 --> 00:06:51,489
"Explain the meaning of the following proverbs."

102
00:06:52,056 --> 00:06:53,992
"50 steps, 100 steps."

103
00:06:54,592 --> 00:06:56,427
Oh, that's easy, right?

104
00:06:59,864 --> 00:07:04,035
Of course, I know. It means...

105
00:07:07,272 --> 00:07:09,407
This is the starting line.

106
00:07:09,741 --> 00:07:12,911
All right, Junpei, walk 100 steps from here.

107
00:07:13,144 --> 00:07:14,045
Okay.

108
00:07:14,412 --> 00:07:16,915
One, two, three, four,

109
00:07:17,148 --> 00:07:21,186
-five, six, seven, eight... -Oh, is that so?

110
00:07:21,686 --> 00:07:25,156
Oh, Ryo-chan, it's dangerous to play on the road.

111
00:07:25,356 --> 00:07:29,194
-Granny, this is for study, got it? -Oh my.

112
00:07:29,928 --> 00:07:31,696
-100 steps. -100 steps.

113
00:07:32,263 --> 00:07:33,765
Finished, Ryo-san!

114
00:07:33,998 --> 00:07:35,200
Okay!

115
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:39,571
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven...

116
00:07:39,771 --> 00:07:42,941
-What's he going to do? -I don't know.

117
00:07:43,474 --> 00:07:46,444
46, 47, 48, 49, 50!

118
00:07:46,644 --> 00:07:47,779
Exactly!

119
00:07:48,012 --> 00:07:49,080
That's right!

120
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:50,882
So, "50 steps, 100 steps" means

121
00:07:51,082 --> 00:07:55,386
when you're a kid, it takes 100 steps, but when you grow up, it's just 50.

122
00:07:55,587 --> 00:07:56,955
Yes, I get it!

123
00:07:59,123 --> 00:08:01,459
I see. That's one interpretation...

124
00:08:01,659 --> 00:08:03,127
That can't be true.

125
00:08:03,328 --> 00:08:04,863
"Eyedrops from the second floor"?

126
00:08:05,396 --> 00:08:08,433
-Hey, Ryo-san! -What does it mean?

127
00:08:08,633 --> 00:08:11,035
Well, we should try it.

128
00:08:11,803 --> 00:08:13,404
I'm ready, Ryo-san!

129
00:08:14,105 --> 00:08:15,506
Okay, just do it!

130
00:08:17,642 --> 00:08:20,044
Aim well.

131
00:08:21,579 --> 00:08:24,215
They really mean to put in eyedrops from the second floor.

132
00:08:35,693 --> 00:08:38,062
We did it!

133
00:08:38,363 --> 00:08:40,131
How was it, Ryo-san? Did you get it?

134
00:08:41,232 --> 00:08:42,600
Ah, it stings!

135
00:08:44,235 --> 00:08:49,073
Putting in eyedrops from the second floor really gives it a boost and feels amazing.

136
00:08:49,274 --> 00:08:50,775
-Hold it, Ryo-chan! -Uh?

137
00:08:51,643 --> 00:08:53,945
-That explanation is totally wrong! -What?

138
00:08:54,345 --> 00:08:56,080
"Eyedrops from the second floor" means

139
00:08:56,281 --> 00:08:59,684
something roundabout, useless, and ineffective.

140
00:08:59,918 --> 00:09:03,187
And "50 steps, 100 steps" is an old Chinese proverb.

141
00:09:03,388 --> 00:09:07,959
A soldier who ran away for 50 steps can't laugh at one who ran for 100 steps.

142
00:09:08,159 --> 00:09:10,528
It means there's really not much difference.

143
00:09:10,728 --> 00:09:13,331
You're not fit to be a tutor!

144
00:09:14,299 --> 00:09:15,266
Hello?

145
00:09:15,733 --> 00:09:19,404
Shut up, Reiko! Keep being that logical and you'll scare off every guy!

146
00:09:19,637 --> 00:09:21,706
What did you just say?

147
00:09:21,939 --> 00:09:23,007
Excuse me...

148
00:09:23,374 --> 00:09:27,946
A neighbor wants us to crack down on illegally parked vehicles.

149
00:09:28,146 --> 00:09:30,114
Reiko-san, will you come with me?

150
00:09:30,315 --> 00:09:31,749
S-Sure.

151
00:09:31,983 --> 00:09:36,187
Listen, Ryo-chan. I'll be back soon. Don't teach them any weird stuff!

152
00:09:36,387 --> 00:09:39,557
Yeah, yeah, I get it. Now go on, get to work.

153
00:09:39,757 --> 00:09:41,025
Take your time and relax.

154
00:09:41,225 --> 00:09:42,060
What?

155
00:09:42,293 --> 00:09:44,062
"OUT ON PATROL"

156
00:09:44,429 --> 00:09:47,065
Now that the noisy one is gone,

157
00:09:47,565 --> 00:09:50,969
don't hesitate to ask me anything you don't understand.

158
00:09:51,169 --> 00:09:52,370
Yes, Ryo-san!

159
00:09:52,570 --> 00:09:53,571
What is it?

160
00:09:54,172 --> 00:09:55,573
What's a crane-turtle problem?

161
00:09:55,973 --> 00:09:57,675
What? A crane-turtle problem?

162
00:09:58,009 --> 00:09:59,177
This one.

163
00:09:59,410 --> 00:10:00,745
Well, what's this?

164
00:10:00,979 --> 00:10:02,347
"There are cranes and turtles.

165
00:10:02,547 --> 00:10:08,086
They have 20 heads and 62 legs in total.

166
00:10:08,319 --> 00:10:11,389
How many cranes and turtles are there?"

167
00:10:11,589 --> 00:10:16,394
Well, a crane has two legs and a turtle has four, so...

168
00:10:19,998 --> 00:10:22,700
It's for the RC! Give it up!

169
00:10:22,900 --> 00:10:25,269
I mean, help me out!

170
00:10:28,206 --> 00:10:31,442
Hey, Ryo-san! Have you caught any cranes?

171
00:10:32,243 --> 00:10:33,778
Shut up!

172
00:10:34,379 --> 00:10:36,481
Boys, how about the turtles?

173
00:10:36,714 --> 00:10:38,616
Yeah, we've got them!

174
00:10:39,017 --> 00:10:41,185
Okay, that should be enough.

175
00:10:47,358 --> 00:10:49,961
Don't get so angry. You're cranes for now.

176
00:10:50,294 --> 00:10:51,596
We have turtles, too.

177
00:10:51,796 --> 00:10:53,798
Now, we can count...

178
00:10:55,133 --> 00:10:56,367
Oh, no!

179
00:10:56,567 --> 00:10:59,137
With their legs inside, we can't count them!

180
00:11:00,471 --> 00:11:02,573
Stop it, no!

181
00:11:02,774 --> 00:11:04,208
No more crane-turtle thing!

182
00:11:04,409 --> 00:11:05,810
Let's study science! Science!

183
00:11:06,044 --> 00:11:08,413
Science is the most important subject!

184
00:11:12,917 --> 00:11:14,452
Is this science?

185
00:11:14,685 --> 00:11:20,158
Yes. The PET bottle rocket works using the law of action and reaction.

186
00:11:20,591 --> 00:11:27,165
That means when you push something, it pushes back just as hard.

187
00:11:27,398 --> 00:11:31,135
You pump a large amount of air into a bottle filled with water,

188
00:11:31,335 --> 00:11:33,638
and when it shoots it out all at once...

189
00:11:36,307 --> 00:11:39,410
The compressed air spurts out water,

190
00:11:39,610 --> 00:11:43,815
and the bottle receives the same amount of force to fly away.

191
00:11:44,015 --> 00:11:47,518
This is the same principle as a real space rocket!

192
00:11:47,852 --> 00:11:50,721
Hey, Ryo-san, can we make a much larger one?

193
00:11:51,355 --> 00:11:53,124
A much larger one?

194
00:11:53,324 --> 00:11:55,526
Okay, let's go advanced!

195
00:11:58,663 --> 00:12:02,033
All right, it's complete. The Ryotsu Drum Can Rocket!

196
00:12:02,266 --> 00:12:03,868
Let's launch it now!

197
00:12:04,102 --> 00:12:05,703
Okay, here we go!

198
00:12:21,052 --> 00:12:23,321
-Ryo-san, all yours! -All yours!

199
00:12:23,521 --> 00:12:25,656
Hey, you cowards!

200
00:12:31,529 --> 00:12:33,364
Ryo-san, are you okay?

201
00:12:33,564 --> 00:12:34,599
Okay?

202
00:12:34,832 --> 00:12:38,202
All right, let's try social studies next.

203
00:12:46,244 --> 00:12:48,579
Turn right down the alley and there's a tofu shop...

204
00:12:54,886 --> 00:12:58,356
Hmm, I didn't know there were so many symbols on the map.

205
00:12:58,556 --> 00:13:00,258
The police station is marked with a cross.

206
00:13:00,491 --> 00:13:02,560
It's a bad omen. A circle would be better.

207
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:06,197
Circles are used for ward offices and town or village offices.

208
00:13:06,864 --> 00:13:08,766
Ah, a ninja mark!

209
00:13:09,367 --> 00:13:12,403
Oh, it's the mark for the Manji Shuriken.

210
00:13:12,803 --> 00:13:17,608
There were also the Cross, Six-Point, and Eight-Point Shuriken.

211
00:13:17,808 --> 00:13:18,976
You know a lot, Ryo-san.

212
00:13:19,210 --> 00:13:22,446
Of course. By the way, I can make the Cross Shuriken with origami.

213
00:13:22,647 --> 00:13:23,881
Really?

214
00:13:30,187 --> 00:13:31,722
There we go!

215
00:13:31,923 --> 00:13:33,190
That's cool!

216
00:13:33,391 --> 00:13:37,228
I used to make this and play ninja. Yah!

217
00:13:40,531 --> 00:13:41,465
Teach me!

218
00:13:41,666 --> 00:13:44,902
Okay! First, fold the origami in half...

219
00:13:49,373 --> 00:13:51,676
Keiichi Nakagawa, reporting back.

220
00:13:51,909 --> 00:13:54,011
Reiko Akimoto, reporting back.

221
00:13:54,245 --> 00:13:55,646
Ah, thanks for your work.

222
00:13:55,846 --> 00:13:57,949
How's the tutor doing?

223
00:13:58,149 --> 00:14:01,219
Well, it looks like they're doing something quietly.

224
00:14:02,687 --> 00:14:04,422
How's their study going, Ryo-chan?

225
00:14:04,622 --> 00:14:05,456
-Wow! -Ouch!

226
00:14:08,693 --> 00:14:11,028
Damn you, Iga ninja!

227
00:14:11,262 --> 00:14:15,032
You think such a wimpy shuriken can hit Ryotsu of Fuma? Take this!

228
00:14:16,767 --> 00:14:19,604
-Prepare to die! -Die, Ryotsu of Fuma!

229
00:14:23,808 --> 00:14:25,509
Just as we thought.

230
00:14:25,710 --> 00:14:28,613
Unbelievable! He's just like a kid!

231
00:14:29,313 --> 00:14:31,249
Take this! Fuma Ninpo, Wild Shot!

232
00:14:32,883 --> 00:14:34,051
Hey, Ryo-chan!

233
00:14:36,053 --> 00:14:36,887
Ryo-chan!

234
00:14:38,122 --> 00:14:39,857
Oh, you're back.

235
00:14:41,692 --> 00:14:42,593
Well, this is...

236
00:14:43,027 --> 00:14:43,894
Gotcha!

237
00:14:45,796 --> 00:14:48,132
S-Struck down...

238
00:14:49,133 --> 00:14:51,369
I'm still... I'm down.

239
00:14:59,010 --> 00:15:00,444
History is easy.

240
00:15:00,645 --> 00:15:03,381
If you memorize it entirely, you're sure to get points.

241
00:15:03,614 --> 00:15:04,448
Okay.

242
00:15:08,052 --> 00:15:11,389
Well, what year were the Taika Reforms?

243
00:15:11,856 --> 00:15:13,658
What? Taika Waititi?

244
00:15:13,924 --> 00:15:17,094
No, the Taika Reforms!

245
00:15:17,495 --> 00:15:20,631
-Gulp! -They were in 645.

246
00:15:21,032 --> 00:15:25,036
To remember 645, think "mu-jiko," Taika reforms for a safer country.

247
00:15:25,236 --> 00:15:27,104
Oh, I see!

248
00:15:27,338 --> 00:15:30,074
There's also that "Treat me like everyone else" thing.

249
00:15:30,308 --> 00:15:33,244
That's how you remember square roots.

250
00:15:34,211 --> 00:15:38,082
-"H, He, Li, Be, my ship..." -That's chemical elements.

251
00:15:39,750 --> 00:15:42,486
There's "Cry, nightingale, Heian-kyo" for 794.

252
00:15:42,687 --> 00:15:45,556
Or "Fueled with passion, Columbus" for 1492.

253
00:15:45,756 --> 00:15:46,891
Yes, that's it!

254
00:15:47,091 --> 00:15:49,126
"Fueled with passion, Columbus"!

255
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:51,696
"Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn..."

256
00:15:51,896 --> 00:15:53,597
"Giants, sumo champ, omelet"

257
00:15:53,798 --> 00:15:58,369
"Oh, Kaneda, Hirooka." Sounds like "Oh, money! Shall I pick it up?"

258
00:15:59,270 --> 00:16:01,372
What the heck are they?

259
00:16:01,572 --> 00:16:03,074
What are you teaching these kids?

260
00:16:03,274 --> 00:16:07,411
That's how I learned as a kid! If you don't like it, tell my teacher!

261
00:16:07,611 --> 00:16:12,750
-Hey, no fair! Tell us what's so fun! -What's so fun?

262
00:16:12,950 --> 00:16:14,685
Oh, I'm sorry.

263
00:16:14,885 --> 00:16:18,723
You remember that 645 was the year of Taika Waititi?

264
00:16:18,923 --> 00:16:21,892
Yeah, next is Ono no Imoko...

265
00:16:22,093 --> 00:16:27,798
Oh, I know him! Everyone used to say, "Ono no Imoko ate a potato and went pfft!"

266
00:16:27,998 --> 00:16:29,734
What a nostalgic name.

267
00:16:29,934 --> 00:16:31,902
He ate a potato and became an envoy?

268
00:16:32,103 --> 00:16:33,971
An envoy?

269
00:16:35,706 --> 00:16:40,077
Wasn't Ono no Imoko just someone who ate potatoes and farted?

270
00:16:40,277 --> 00:16:43,080
So why is his name in history?

271
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:45,783
Because he was the first in Japan to eat a potato and fart.

272
00:16:45,983 --> 00:16:47,118
I've had enough!

273
00:16:47,318 --> 00:16:50,821
-Aw, I'm not gonna get 80. -No way.

274
00:16:54,558 --> 00:16:57,161
Was there an envoy to the Tang Dynasty too?

275
00:16:57,394 --> 00:17:00,731
Yes, there was. It was about 20 years after the Sui Dynasty one.

276
00:17:00,931 --> 00:17:03,167
There must have been an envoy ship to the Tang Dynasty.

277
00:17:03,401 --> 00:17:06,604
Right, it was used to go to China.

278
00:17:08,572 --> 00:17:11,175
Didn't that ship look like this?

279
00:17:11,742 --> 00:17:13,844
The one with a lot of people rowing.

280
00:17:14,044 --> 00:17:16,580
Wow! I think it probably looked like that.

281
00:17:16,781 --> 00:17:18,649
Ryo-chan, you remember well!

282
00:17:18,849 --> 00:17:21,018
Yeah, I'm starting to remember.

283
00:17:21,218 --> 00:17:26,490
I used to draw U-boats firing torpedoes at the envoy ship in my textbook.

284
00:17:26,690 --> 00:17:29,493
-Wow, that's good! -Cool!

285
00:17:30,060 --> 00:17:32,830
But how do you remember all the details of the ship?

286
00:17:33,030 --> 00:17:35,766
I've copied the ship and drawn it so many times.

287
00:17:35,966 --> 00:17:37,501
I can draw the Kanrin Maru, too.

288
00:17:37,701 --> 00:17:42,773
The Kanrin Maru was a small wooden warship about 50 meters long, built in Holland.

289
00:17:42,973 --> 00:17:43,974
Whoa!

290
00:17:44,175 --> 00:17:47,244
I'm sure it was used as a training ship for the Shogunate Navy.

291
00:17:47,478 --> 00:17:49,380
It had five cannons on each side.

292
00:17:49,713 --> 00:17:51,182
You know a lot about it.

293
00:17:51,382 --> 00:17:55,186
Someone went to the U.S. on this ship. Who was it?

294
00:17:55,386 --> 00:17:56,921
Not Katsu Shintaro, but...

295
00:17:57,154 --> 00:17:58,155
Katsu Kaishu, right?

296
00:17:58,522 --> 00:17:59,657
Oh, yes, that's him!

297
00:17:59,924 --> 00:18:03,160
You don't know about history, but you sure remember the pictures.

298
00:18:03,661 --> 00:18:06,363
I can draw people, too. How about Commodore Perry?

299
00:18:06,564 --> 00:18:08,399
Perry?

300
00:18:08,632 --> 00:18:10,701
Well, I think he looks like this.

301
00:18:10,901 --> 00:18:13,103
-Wearing a military uniform... -Wow! Amazing!

302
00:18:13,337 --> 00:18:15,105
Yeah, I think it looks like him.

303
00:18:15,339 --> 00:18:16,941
How can you draw so quickly?

304
00:18:17,174 --> 00:18:21,412
It was in the textbook. I used to doodle like this all the time during class.

305
00:18:25,115 --> 00:18:26,851
There was also Sugita Genpaku.

306
00:18:27,051 --> 00:18:28,919
In Ukiyo-e style, he'd look like this.

307
00:18:30,120 --> 00:18:31,522
Pretty good, isn't it?

308
00:18:31,922 --> 00:18:36,393
This kind of head was the most fun to doodle on, and I enjoyed it at the time.

309
00:18:37,862 --> 00:18:41,899
-Ryo-san, can you draw Yoritomo? -How about Hideyoshi?

310
00:18:42,132 --> 00:18:43,400
Yeah, of course!

311
00:18:47,872 --> 00:18:53,577
I can draw Ieyasu, Nobunaga, and Francisco Xavier!

312
00:18:54,745 --> 00:18:57,615
Ryotsu, do you know who Sugita Genpaku is?

313
00:18:58,215 --> 00:19:00,618
He must be a rakugo storyteller.

314
00:19:01,151 --> 00:19:04,121
He's the guy who wrote the famous Kaitai Shinsho!

315
00:19:06,857 --> 00:19:10,761
Oh, judging from his appearance, I thought he was a rakugo storyteller.

316
00:19:11,161 --> 00:19:13,797
So he's the one who wrote Yajikita Dochuki.

317
00:19:13,998 --> 00:19:16,133
No, that was Jippensha Ikku.

318
00:19:18,235 --> 00:19:20,604
Well, this turned into an unexpected lesson.

319
00:19:20,804 --> 00:19:24,141
Don't blame me if he fails the tests.

320
00:19:25,876 --> 00:19:27,945
Oh, no! Don't draw on that!

321
00:19:30,915 --> 00:19:32,016
"WANTED"

322
00:19:33,450 --> 00:19:35,352
That's a pretty good drawing!

323
00:19:35,719 --> 00:19:38,255
This is because you teach boring stuff, Ryo-chan!

324
00:19:38,455 --> 00:19:40,491
You were impressed, too.

325
00:19:40,824 --> 00:19:43,961
That's all for today's lesson. Ding-dong!

326
00:19:44,295 --> 00:19:46,463
Hey, what about the RC?

327
00:19:46,931 --> 00:19:47,965
It can't be helped.

328
00:19:48,165 --> 00:19:51,001
This is just too much of a prank.

329
00:19:51,335 --> 00:19:52,903
Ryo-chan, bring them back!

330
00:19:53,103 --> 00:19:54,204
What, me?

331
00:19:54,438 --> 00:19:57,808
Teaching them not to do these things is part of the lesson!

332
00:19:58,342 --> 00:19:59,310
Okay...

333
00:20:02,379 --> 00:20:05,516
Where the heck did they go?

334
00:20:07,751 --> 00:20:10,054
No, it can't be...

335
00:20:14,525 --> 00:20:16,327
Oh no!

336
00:20:16,660 --> 00:20:18,829
-Hey, Ryo-san, is it a case? -Shut up!

337
00:20:22,032 --> 00:20:23,500
Hey, I found you!

338
00:20:23,701 --> 00:20:26,003
Whoa, Ryo-san!

339
00:20:26,337 --> 00:20:28,138
Knock it off, you brats!

340
00:20:28,639 --> 00:20:30,407
Don't get cocky!

341
00:20:30,641 --> 00:20:32,176
I'm sorry.

342
00:20:32,376 --> 00:20:34,378
Oh, Ryo-san, look!

343
00:20:34,678 --> 00:20:39,149
-I'm not falling for that! -But he looks just like Junpei's doodle!

344
00:20:41,251 --> 00:20:42,953
Th-That man!

345
00:20:45,422 --> 00:20:47,091
Hey, Tatsu the Viper, huh?

346
00:20:47,625 --> 00:20:51,328
I knew it! He was in disguise!

347
00:20:54,231 --> 00:20:55,065
Hey, stop!

348
00:20:58,836 --> 00:21:00,871
I won't let you get away!

349
00:21:10,447 --> 00:21:12,883
Yo, Ryo-san, you're the best in Japan!

350
00:21:15,552 --> 00:21:17,388
Tatsu the Viper, you're under arrest!

351
00:21:19,023 --> 00:21:21,191
How did you know?

352
00:21:24,828 --> 00:21:27,665
Well, that was totally unexpected!

353
00:21:28,899 --> 00:21:32,036
Not at all! I had a feeling this might happen,

354
00:21:32,236 --> 00:21:34,938
so I taught them how fun doodling can be!

355
00:21:35,139 --> 00:21:36,073
Real slick!

356
00:21:36,540 --> 00:21:39,677
If he aced the tests too, there's nothing else to say.

357
00:21:39,910 --> 00:21:42,413
You idiot! Of course, he nailed them!

358
00:21:42,613 --> 00:21:45,282
Who do you think taught him, huh?

359
00:21:47,251 --> 00:21:48,786
Ryo-san!

360
00:21:51,088 --> 00:21:52,456
Look at this!

361
00:21:52,689 --> 00:21:54,458
Oh, you got 80!

362
00:21:54,958 --> 00:21:56,960
No, my highest score was 50.

363
00:21:57,327 --> 00:22:00,064
You're 30 points short. Why?

364
00:22:00,964 --> 00:22:05,169
I helped catch the criminal, so a big shot from the police treated me!

365
00:22:05,502 --> 00:22:07,171
-Good for you. -Yeah!

366
00:22:11,775 --> 00:22:15,079
Not all studying is done behind a desk.

367
00:22:15,279 --> 00:22:18,949
My practical study method is the true studying.

368
00:22:19,149 --> 00:22:19,983
Right!

369
00:22:20,184 --> 00:22:25,189
For example, our chief only focused on studying, which made his mind so stiff.

370
00:22:25,422 --> 00:22:27,958
He doesn't even twitch a muscle watching TV variety shows!

371
00:22:28,158 --> 00:22:29,326
He ends up getting angry.

372
00:22:29,593 --> 00:22:30,961
W-Wait, Ryotsu...

373
00:22:32,663 --> 00:22:34,198
But it's true!

374
00:22:34,431 --> 00:22:36,600
With that thick head, no one will follow him.

375
00:22:36,999 --> 00:22:38,669
He's just a stubborn old man.

376
00:22:38,902 --> 00:22:40,671
-Ryotsu-kun. -Gulp!

377
00:22:42,906 --> 00:22:44,141
C-Chief!

378
00:22:44,341 --> 00:22:46,210
You did a great job yesterday.

379
00:22:46,477 --> 00:22:51,215
You're a fine officer for working with the public to arrest a wanted criminal.

380
00:22:51,448 --> 00:22:58,155
But I'd be grateful if you could clean up that "practical study" graffiti too.

381
00:22:59,323 --> 00:23:01,959
Come on, that's a tough joke, Chief.

382
00:23:02,159 --> 00:23:03,327
They did that, not me...

383
00:23:03,927 --> 00:23:06,330
Stop complaining and just go clean up!

384
00:23:06,530 --> 00:23:07,765
Oh no!

385
00:23:11,568 --> 00:23:14,138
Why do I have to do such a thing?

386
00:23:14,571 --> 00:23:17,241
Hey, Ryo-san, I heard you did a good job!

387
00:23:19,109 --> 00:23:21,845
Hey, you guys, help me out!

388
00:23:23,547 --> 00:23:29,019
Ryosan, we're gonna play with the RC in the park. Come over when you're done!

389
00:23:29,219 --> 00:23:30,721
Come over!

390
00:23:31,822 --> 00:23:33,323
Damn those kids!

391
00:23:33,524 --> 00:23:36,560
Ah, this is ridiculous! I can't do this!

392
00:23:37,060 --> 00:23:41,198
No, it's fun to clean up.

393
00:23:41,965 --> 00:23:44,401
Ryotsu-kun, I forgot to tell you earlier,

394
00:23:44,601 --> 00:23:49,173
but I've decided to deduct the cost of the display window from your salary.
